  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN262.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">iravukkuṟikkaṇ talaimakaḷaip puṇarntu nīṅkun talaimakaṉ taṉ neñciṟkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What HE, who left after having united with HER during the night tryst, said to his heart.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN262.1">
        <l>mutaipaṭu pacuṅkā ṭariṟpava<supplied>r ma</supplied>yakkip</l>
        <l>pakaṭupala pūṇṭa vuḻavuṟu <supplied>ce</supplied>ñce</l>
        <l>yiṭumuṟai nirampi yākuviṉaik kalittup</l>
        <l>pācilai yamaṉṟa payaṟūḻ <anchor n="1"/>pukkeṉa</l>
        <l>vāymoḻit tattaiyaik kaṇkaḷain taruḷā</l>
        <l>tūrmutu kō<supplied>car na</supplied>vaitta ciṟumaiyiṟ</l>
        <l>kalattu muṇṇāḷ vālitu muṭā<supplied>a</supplied>ḷ</l>
        <l>ciṉattiṟ koṇṭa <anchor n="2"/>paṭiva māṟāḷ</l>
        <l>maṟaṅkeḻu tāṉaik koṟṟak kuṟumpiyaṉ</l>
        <l>ceruviya ṉaṉmara ṉaṟitiyāka kuraittava</l>
        <l>riṉṉuyir cekuppak kaṇṭuciṉa māṟiya</l>
        <l>vaṉṉi miñili pōla <anchor n="3"/>meymmalin</l>
        <l>tāṉā <supplied>vu</supplied>va<supplied>kai</supplied>yē māyiṉēm pūmalin</l>
        <l>taruvi yārkku mayantikaḻ cilampi </l>
        <l>ṉuṇpaḵ ṟuvalai putaṉmicai naṉaikkum</l>
        <l>vaṇṭupaṭu naṟaviṉ <anchor n="4"/>vaṇmakiḻp <anchor n="5"/>pēkaṉ</l>
        <l>koṇṭakaṉ māmalai nāṟi</l>
        <l>yantīṅ kaḷvi vanta <supplied>mā</supplied>ṟē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="4">Because the green-gram thickly grown with green leaves entered [the state of] ripeness,</l>
        <l corresp="3">grown by work in progress, maturing in the order they had been put</l>
        <l corresp="2">on the red field that underwent ploughing for which many bulls were yoked,</l>
        <l corresp="1">mixed with the interlacing creepers of the green wilderness that creeps back of old,</l>
        <l corresp="5">without deigning to rid the area from true-worded  parakeets, </l>
        <l corresp="12">[her] body flourishing like Aṉṉi Miñili,</l>
        <l corresp="11">who swerved from [his] anger when he saw the sweet life destroyed</l>
        <l corresp="10">of those who revelled, as you would know, at the war-like good tree</l>
        <l corresp="9">of victorious Kuṟumpiyaṉ  with the valourous army</l>
        <l corresp="8">of her who does not change from the form she had taken in anger,</l>
        <l corresp="7">who does not eat from vessels and does not put on anything pure,</l>
        <l corresp="6">because of a small thing that was killed by the ancient Kōcar [in their] village(?),</l>
        <l corresp="13a-c">we are filled with unending joy,</l>
        <l corresp="18">because the pretty sweet robber has come,</l>
        <l corresp="17">the wide big mountain being fragrant, taken by</l>
        <l corresp="16">delightful Pēkaṉ, liberal with toddy sought by bees,</l>
        <l corresp="15">where many fine drops wet the tops of bushes,</l>
        <l corresp="14">on the water-glittering mountain side, where waterfalls roar,</l>
        <l corresp="13d">abounding in flowers.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

